'''Metal Cyclone''' (メタルサイクロン, ''Metaru Saikuron'', '''Metal Cyclone''') is a [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemy and [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]] introduced in [[Attack on Titanium (Insane)|Sweet Irony]].
{{Enemy Info
|name = Metal Cyclone
|image = E 071.png
|appearance = [[Attack on Titanium (Insane)|Sweet Irony]]<br>'''ZL''': [[Groundscraper|Sub-chapter 11 - Groundscraper]]
|money drop = 3,000¢ - 11,850¢
}}

==Enemy==
Similarly to other [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]]s, this very slow enemy attacks non-stop and deals extreme damage, but has a tiny range of 65. It takes only 1 damage from non-[[Critical Hit|Critical]] attacks like all Metal enemies yet has more than triple the health of [[Sir Metal Seal]], requiring a lot of [[Critical Hit]]s to defeat. Fortunately, Metal Cyclone does have a very high knockback count, making it easy to keep at bay if enough damage is dealt to it.

==Strategy==
Depending on the support, you may have to reserve only a few [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metal]] specialists to take it down. When using [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critters]] like [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Jurassic Cat Sitter]] that value quantity over quality, it's important to back them with [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-control units]] so they could at least attack it with impunity. Guaranteed Critical units like [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Waitress Cat]], while definitely useful, will also require support so they don't waste their powerful Critical Hits on something else.

